  era: "c. 7000 BCE onwards \xB7 Section 1 \xB7 Prehistoric India \xB7 c. 1.5 million years ago \u2013 700 BCE"
  title: Neolithic agriculture
  text: At Mehrgarh, early farmers grew barley and wheat. Rice was cultivated in the Ganga valley, for example at Lahuradewa, and millets and pulses in the south. Farming produced surpluses that let people settle and populations grow.
